    en: {
      title: 'Errors, rollback, and disposal',
      lede: 'Close fields and distinguish primary failures, rollback errors, and shared-instance failure.',
      document: {
        sections: [
          {
            id: 'dispose',
            heading: 'An old field cannot be read after page closure',
            blocks: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'First save load-wasm.ts from [getting started](/en/docs/store-wasm/getting-started), then place this page’s entry beside it. The helper loads the package’s actual WASM in Node and waits for field initialization.'
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'A component may retain its score field reference. Closing the store also disposes that field. Handle the error and stop using the old reference rather than reuse it on a new page.'
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Save as `dispose.ts`.'
              },
              {
                type: 'code',
                language: 'ts',
                code: "import './load-wasm.ts'\nimport { createStore } from '@migaia/store-light'\nimport * as wasm from '@migaia/store-wasm'\n\nconst store = createStore({ score: wasm.number() })\nconst score = store.score\nscore.value = 9\nawait store.$dispose()\ntry {\n  void score.value\n} catch (error) {\n  const failure = error as { code: string }\n  console.log('Score read after page close:', failure.code)\n}"
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Output:'
              },
              {
                type: 'code',
                language: 'text',
                code: 'Score read after page close: FIELD_DISPOSED'
              },
              {
                type: 'table',
                headers: ['Member or option', 'Description'],
                rows: [
                  [
                    '`store.$dispose(): Promise<void>`',
                    'The store closes its WASM fields. Export any needed data first, then await store disposal.'
                  ],
                  [
                    '`field.dispose(): void`',
                    'When calling builder.create directly, the caller closes the field. Disposal marks it closed, unregisters fallback cleanup, then releases tracking objects and the memory block.'
                  ],
                  [
                    '`field.disposed: boolean`',
                    'Becomes true when disposal starts. Repeated disposal has no extra effect and does not retry cleanup that failed on the first call.'
                  ],
                  [
                    'Reads after disposal',
                    'Scalar value access fails, but observed and disposed remain readable. Arrays retain readable length and disposed properties.'
                  ]
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            id: 'rollback',
            heading: 'Retain construction and cleanup failures',
            blocks: [
              {
                type: 'table',
                headers: ['Member or option', 'Description'],
                rows: [
                  [
                    'Construction rollback',
                    'If tracking setup fails after allocation, acquired resources enter rollback. When setup and cleanup both fail, retain both as described below.'
                  ],
                  [
                    'Mutable primary error',
                    'Append the rollback cleanup failure to the original error’s non-enumerable errors, preserve cause, and throw that original error.'
                  ],
                  [
                    'Primary cannot accept details',
                    'For a primitive, frozen, or otherwise unwritable primary, throw a CLEANUP_FAILED aggregate with the primary first.'
                  ],
                  [
                    'Normal disposal failures',
                    'One cleanup failure is thrown unchanged. Multiple failures become a CLEANUP_FAILED AggregateError retaining execution order. This differs from construction rollback attachment.'
                  ],
                  [
                    'Garbage-collection fallback',
                    'FinalizationRegistry is an optional fallback with unpredictable timing. It does not replace normal store or caller disposal.'
                  ]
                ]
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'The errors attachment rule applies to package primary-plus-rollback failures, including failed byte rollback in setRange. Normal disposal follows its own single-or-multiple cleanup rule; cause is not a universal cleanup location.'
              },
              {
                type: 'table',
                headers: ['Member or option', 'Description'],
                rows: [
                  [
                    '`NOT_INITIALIZED`',
                    'Synchronous field creation ran before initialization. Await successful ensureWasm before creating fields.'
                  ],
                  [
                    '`FIELD_DISPOSED`',
                    'Accessed a closed field or called a closed array method. Create a new field rather than reuse it.'
                  ],
                  [
                    '`INIT_ABORTED`',
                    'The initialization signal is cancelled. An extensible untagged native reason keeps its identity and type, including AbortError, with INIT_ABORTED attached. Frozen or non-Error reasons remain reachable through cause; complete foreign error identities keep their owner.'
                  ],
                  [
                    '`RESERVED_FIELD_NAME`',
                    'A record key conflicts with dispose or disposed. Rename the business field.'
                  ],
                  [
                    '`ALLOCATION_FAILED`',
                    'Allocation returned invalid markers, array alignment failed, or stored string length is corrupt. Check capacity and data. Allocation failure does not itself imply a trap.'
                  ],
                  [
                    '`INVALID_OPTION`',
                    'Invalid capacity, granularity, index, range, value type, or oversized text. Correct the argument rather than retry identical input.'
                  ],
                  [
                    '`CLEANUP_FAILED`',
                    'Aggregates multiple release failures or rollback failures when details cannot be attached to the primary. Inspect retained errors.'
                  ],
                  [
                    '`INSTANCE_POISONED`',
                    'Later allocation after an arena WebAssembly.RuntimeError fails with this code and the first trap as cause. Reload the page or restart the process.'
                  ]
                ]
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Only a native RuntimeError from arena allocation, pointer lookup, or release marks the instance failed. The first trap is rethrown unchanged; later allocations fail with INSTANCE_POISONED, and releases skip the arena.'
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'EnsureWasm still returns its cache and cannot repair the failed instance. Existing field accesses do not uniformly change to the poisoning error.'
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            id: 'tools',
            heading: 'Error and field-mode tools',
            blocks: [
              {
                type: 'table',
                headers: ['Member or option', 'Description'],
                rows: [
                  [
                    '`STORE_WASM_SOURCE`',
                    'Package-created errors use this source string. A first native trap or external tracking error can pass through unchanged without a package code.'
                  ],
                  [
                    '`StoreWasmErrorCode` / `IStoreWasmErrorCode`',
                    'Runtime constants and value type for the eight codes above.'
                  ],
                  [
                    '`createStoreWasmError(code, message, options?: { cause?: unknown }): Error`',
                    'Creates a coded Error with the package source and preserves a supplied cause.'
                  ],
                  [
                    '`createStoreWasmRangeError(code, message): RangeError`',
                    'Creates a tagged RangeError. There is no third cause-options argument.'
                  ],
                  [
                    '`createStoreWasmTypeError(code, message, options?: { cause?: unknown }): TypeError`',
                    'Creates a tagged TypeError and preserves a supplied cause.'
                  ],
                  [
                    '`createStoreWasmAggregateError(code, errors: readonly unknown[], message): AggregateError`',
                    'Creates an aggregate retaining every original error. Usually used by extension authors; applications handle existing failures.'
                  ],
                  [
                    '`WasmReservedKey` / `IWasmReservedKey`',
                    'Constants and value type for the record lifecycle names dispose and disposed.'
                  ]
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      next: [
        {
          label: 'Choose ordinary or WASM fields',
          path: 'performance-and-when-not-to-use'
        },
        {
          label: 'Initialization and readiness',
          path: 'initialization-and-provider-readiness'
        }
      ]
    }
